---
name: acos-propagate-<PROJECT_NAME>
description: Propagate entrypoint renames for <PROJECT_NAME> across in-scope and out-of-scope references.
---

<objective>
Propagate pending entrypoint renames (route: <ROUTE_SUMMARY>) for <PROJECT_NAME> across all reference locations, including those outside the deterministic scanner's `.ssot/` root. This skill is analysis output made actionable: it does not widen the agent's write authority (REQ-055) and does not mutate any file outside the skill directory during generation.
</objective>

<when_to_load>
- When `530-migrate-refs` is dispatched and this skill exists at `.ssot/skills/acos-propagate-<PROJECT_NAME>/` (REQ-053).
- Before updating any reference to a renamed entrypoint.
- When a fresh agent arrives on an already-initialized project with a pending version migration.
</when_to_load>

<essential_principles>
<principle name="rename_mapping_first">
Read `references/rename-mapping.md` before touching any reference. The mapping defines old→new visible prefix, stable ID, and slug.
</principle>

<principle name="in_scope_advisory">
In-scope references (under `.ssot/`) in `references/ref-report.md` are an advisory snapshot. Refresh at dispatch time with `acos --check --refs-only` (REQ-054).
</principle>

<principle name="out_of_scope_enumerated">
Out-of-scope references are enumerated in `references/out-of-scope-locations.md` with a per-location classification. This is content the generic dispatch payload cannot produce.
</principle>

<principle name="preserve_verbatim">
Locations classified `preserve-verbatim` MUST NOT be modified (REQ-055). They are historical or explanatory references that intentionally name an old prefix.
</principle>

<principle name="no_widened_authority">
Out-of-scope updates require explicit human approval. The post-agent diff check (REQ-026) still governs in-scope references. Generating this skill did not update any reference in the target project.
</principle>

<principle name="freshness">
Verify freshness via `provenance.json` before acting. If the project changed after generation, request regeneration.
</principle>
</essential_principles>

<reference_index>
- `references/rename-mapping.md` — old→new prefixes, stable IDs, slugs.
- `references/ref-report.md` — in-scope references (advisory snapshot).
- `references/out-of-scope-locations.md` — references outside `.ssot/` with classification.
- `references/conventions.md` — how this project references entrypoints.
- `references/protected-paths.md` — paths that must not be modified.
- `references/decisions.md` — durable project decisions.
</reference_index>

<workflows_index>
| Workflow | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `workflows/propagate.md` | Step-by-step propagation procedure. |
</workflows_index>

<success_criteria>
This skill is used correctly when:
- All in-scope references refreshed and updated deterministically.
- Out-of-scope `update` locations updated with explicit human approval.
- `preserve-verbatim` locations left untouched.
- `needs-human-judgment` locations presented for review and resolved.
- Post-agent diff check (REQ-026) passes.
- `npx acos --validate` and `npx acos --check` pass.
</success_criteria>
